 ## Overview
-This method renders voxel chunks as triangle meshes using a horizontal texture atlas for block faces, applying per-vertex ambient occlusion (AO) and smooth light in the fragment shader with directional lighting [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [Naive Voxel Meshing](2376-naive-voxel-meshing.md) by using a shared atlas to reduce texture bind calls, and from [GPU Marching Cubes (Face-based)](3674-gpu-marching-cubes-face-based.md) by relying on axis-aligned quads rather than isosurfaces [S1, unofficial].
+This method renders voxel chunks as triangle meshes by mapping block faces to a horizontal texture atlas and applying per-vertex lighting in the fragment shader. It builds on [Voxel Chunk Meshing with Culling](2523-voxel-chunk-meshing-with-culling.md) to generate geometry, then optimizes rendering by batching materials into a single atlas and computing lighting values (ambient occlusion and smooth light) at the vertex level. Unlike [Naive Voxel Meshing](2376-naive-voxel-meshing.md) which may use separate textures or per-face lighting, this approach reduces texture bind calls and supports complex block shapes (slabs, stairs) via specific UV offsets.
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs and Outputs**
-- **Input**: A voxel chunk, a set of 16×16 tile images for block faces, and camera matrices [S1, unofficial].
-- **Output**: A rendered image containing opaque, two-sided, and transparent geometry [S1, unofficial].
 
-**Data Structures**
-The vertex structure contains the following fields [S1, unofficial]:
-- `pos`: `Vec4<f32>` (position in world space, w=1.0).
-- `uv`: `Vec2<f32>` (local UV coordinates within the tile, typically 0.0 to 1.0).
-- `normal`: `Vec3<f32>` (face normal).
-- `ao`: `f32` (ambient occlusion, normalized).
-- `smooth_light`: `f32` (smooth lighting value, normalized).
-- `block`: `MyBlock` (enum identifying the block type).
-- `atlas_offset`: `f32` (U-offset in the atlas strip, representing the tile index).
-- `two_sided`: `bool` (flag for backface culling behavior).
